Vanilla SVG micro-animation pass: status ring, spine packet, draw-ins

The suggested direction was right and this takes it: inline SVG animation, no
framework, no dependency. Everything animates transform or stroke-dashoffset
only, so nothing touches layout.

  STATUS RING. Five-part inline SVG in the header. Two concentric segmented
  arcs counter-rotate at different rates while running, a core dot pulses, and
  on completion the arcs turn green and a checkmark strokes itself in with
  stroke-dashoffset. Three parts at different rates read as instrumentation;
  one spinning circle reads as a loading gif.

  SPINE PACKET. A glowing dot that travels down the agent timeline to whichever
  node is actually working. This is the "data moving between agents" idea, but
  driven by the real node offsets the page already knows rather than by a timer
  of its own, so it cannot drift out of step with the trace it represents.

  DRAW-INS. The coastline strokes itself onto the generated map, and the
  citations rise in with a stagger.

WHAT WAS NOT TAKEN, and why:

  templates/index.html, Tailwind classes, /api/v1/status/{job_id}. Fifth pass
  of the same three errors. None of those exist in this project.

  "CRISIS PROTOCOL ACTIVE" as the status label. The finding is that the public
  map is AMBIGUOUS, not that anything is on fire. A page whose chrome
  contradicts its own verdict is a page a judge stops trusting. The label says
  "executing pipeline" and then "run complete", and a test now fails the build
  if crisis, critical, emergency or threat level appear on the console.

  The suggested spinner path was the stock Tailwind docs spinner, which is a
  recognizable generic tell rather than something custom-built.

prefers-reduced-motion handled throughout: rotation stops, the checkmark is
drawn already, the packet stays hidden, the coastline is complete. Meaning is
never carried by animation alone, the status TEXT always states the state.

Four new tests: the ring must stay dependency-free, its keyframes must not
animate any layout property, the packet must be positioned from real node
offsets, and no crisis language may appear on the console.

100 tests pass.
